---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Behavior Adjustment Training San Jacinto | Good Doggos";
const description = "Sophisticated behavior adjustment training in San Jacinto. Stop being the owner who has to hide and start building confidence through leadership.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Behavior Adjustment Training",
  "description": description,
  "provider": {
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "name": "Good Doggos",
    "url": "https://gooddoggos.com",
    "telephone": "+19514016252",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "San Jacinto",
      "addressRegion": "CA",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    "name": "Riverside County"
  },
  "url": "https://gooddoggos.com/services/behavior-adjustment-training"
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero Band -->
  <section class="bg-primary-navy pt-32 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-body text-white/50 mt-6 mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Home</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="/services/behavioral-modification" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Behavioral Modification</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <span class="text-white/80 truncate">Behavior Adjustment Training</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        Behavior Adjustment Training in San Jacinto
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="py-16 px-4 bg-[#FCF9FA]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          If you feel like you’re holding a live grenade every time you clip on a leash, you aren’t alone. It’s a special kind of stress when your dog's first instinct at the sight of another dog is to go "nuclear"—barking, lunging, and spinning until your shoulders ache.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          These "Red Zone" reactions are symptoms of a dog that hasn't learned they have choices other than fight or flight. Because we are professionals, we do not guess or hand out generic advice. We must evaluate your dog in person to build a sophisticated plan that bridges the gap between "management" and true reliability.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-primary-navy mt-12 mb-6">
          Creating Choices Through Leadership
        </h2>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          At Good Doggos, I take a more sophisticated approach. I use Behavior Adjustment Training principles, but with the backbone of a balanced system. The goal is to teach your dog that they have choices other than "fight or flight." My confidence in these "Red Zone" cases comes from my own journey—after being attacked by a dog as a child in Mexico, I had to master dog behavior strategies to overcome my fear. I felt empowered once I could stop a fight using leadership rather than force.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          Take Camila, a reactive Pitbull/Boxer mix labeled as "un-trainable." In her sessions, she learned that jumping and challenging other dogs had consequences, but respecting space brought peace. My helper dog Simba was key here—his calm, measured corrections provided the "interrupt" she needed to finally listen. 
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          We don't train in a vacuum. We take the work to where the triggers live, from a quiet corner of Hoffman Park to busier San Jacinto streets. In our extreme summer heat, you don't want to be wrestling a reactive dog; you want a dog that checks in with you. By blending positive reinforcement with fair, physical communication, we bridge the gap between "management" and true reliability.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6 font-bold">
          Stop being the owner who has to hide. Let’s build your dog's confidence and your own.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA BAND
══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#FBF1E9]" style="border-top: 1px solid #E6DAC6;">
  <div class="w-full h-[3px]" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #0F6D72, #D1B27F, #0F6D72);"></div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: rgba(15,109,114,0.60);">Your Dog Is Next</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4" style="color: #0B2744;">
      Ready to See What's Possible?<br/>
      <span class="headline-accent" style="color: #D1B27F; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700;">Start With a Free Assessment.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.60);">
      Tell us about your dog. We'll do an honest assessment and point you toward the right program — or tell you if we're not the right fit.
    </p>
    <a href="/apply"
       class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-bold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
       style="background: #D1B27F; color: #0B2744; padding: 18px 44px; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(209,178,127,0.35);">
      Apply for Free Behavioral Assessment →
    </a>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.40);">Takes less than 3 minutes · No commitment required</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
